---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Live Object Repeats"
  description="Create editable grid, radial, and mirror repeats from a shared group source in Varve."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="live-repeat-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Live Object Repeats
      </nav>

      <header class="feature-heading">
        <StatusPill status="experimental" label="Source-build preview" />
        <h1>Repeat the group. Keep its source editable.</h1>
        <p class="feature-intro">
          Grid, radial, and mirror arrangements stay attached to a group. Change its source
          artwork, then tune the repeat in the Inspector without replacing the authored shapes with
          a pile of copies.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="repeat-controls">
        <h2 id="repeat-controls">Three arrangements, one source group</h2>
        <div class="capability-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Grid</h3>
            <p>Set row and column counts and horizontal or vertical spacing.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Radial</h3>
            <p>Set the instance count, sweep, and rotation center. A full turn avoids a doubled seam.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Mirror</h3>
            <p>Choose either or both local axes and set the reflection center.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p>
          The children remain the authored source. Selecting a repeated group exposes numeric
          controls in the Inspector; editing a source child updates the evaluated instances. The
          repeat recipe is part of the document model and survives codec save/reopen.
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="boundary-card" aria-labelledby="repeat-boundaries">
        <h2 id="repeat-boundaries">Current boundaries</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Repeat placement is edited numerically in the Inspector; direct canvas handles are not available yet.</li>
          <li>Release or expand into independent artwork is not available yet.</li>
          <li>Generation is capped at 512 instances to bound render and hit-test work.</li>
          <li>SVG, PDF, and raster export fidelity for object repeats has not been independently qualified. This page makes no interchange editability claim.</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>

      <p class="related-link">
        Object repeats arrange scene artwork. See <a href={sitePath('/features/patterns')}>reusable
        patterns</a> for repeating paint inside a shape with a separate definition workflow.
      </p>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .live-repeat-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--type-interface-readout-size);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .breadcrumb a,
  .related-link a {
    color: var(--text-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
  }

  .feature-heading h1 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: var(--type-marketing-hero-size);
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .feature-intro {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--type-content-lead-size);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .feature-section,
  .boundary-card {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .feature-section h2,
  .boundary-card h2 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: var(--type-display-section-size);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .feature-section p,
  .boundary-card li,
  .related-link {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .capability-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(13rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .capability-grid article,
  .boundary-card {
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: var(--website-radius-card);
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .capability-grid h3 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .capability-grid p,
  .boundary-card ul {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .boundary-card li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .related-link {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
